                        "entry_id": "57e989f1-a45f-36c8-8bb1-a4f126482b75",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having much scenery; scenic."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5463f361-5081-4807-931a-1cd7e96dc871",
                                "sense_id": "1ed6321e-4fcc-3654-ac23-d1b636c49897",
                                "text": "Clad in the verdure of unnumber'd isles, Where scepter'd William's massy bulwarks stand, The guard and glory of the sceneful land."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0abcedc1-b53c-445b-8633-06318edfbd84",
                                "sense_id": "1ed6321e-4fcc-3654-ac23-d1b636c49897",
                                "text": "He never came to view the sceneful world with the minuteness and understanding of a later poet who could describe The Man who slices lemons into drink, The coffee-roaster's brasier, and the boys That volunteer to help him turn its winch."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6a14de3-9178-4b7f-a957-ac293e4460a5",
                                "sense_id": "1ed6321e-4fcc-3654-ac23-d1b636c49897",
                                "text": "In proper midcentury fashion, Collins “view[s] that Oak, the fancied Glades among,” views the indolent, sightless Milton, views the whole Edenic mount in his wildly sceneful fancy."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
